t me  he was clearly intoxicated as soon as I  figured out where the door was I made a  mad dash for the exit which may have in  fact been an entrance because it led me  to a dimly lit locker room I guess that  if that was one time pool for employees  that this must be the corresponding  locker room the lockers were pretty  small and most of them were open and  empty the only sound I could hear was  that of running water on the far side of  the locker room in the dark after all  that I had experienced I thought it  might be best to approach the door on  the other side of the room more  stealthily I was also feeling very sick  and needed to catch my breath I still  felt like I was going to pass out I walk  over to the source of the water keeping  my footsteps as quiet as possible  there are a few shower stalls up ahead I  poked my head into the first and it's  empty I proceeded continuing to check on  the second third and fourth stalls but  what I see in the fourth stall stops me  dead in my tracks in the corner of the  shower an old man stands in the showers  stream he's naked  senile and borderline deformed and he  has his head buried in the corner  luckily he doesn't seem to notice me so  I decided to tiptoe past him to get to  the door I make it across safely but as  I gripped the door handle I hear a  terrifying cry out from behind me I see  you you'll never get me out of here  you're the one who has to go  I hear wet footsteps charging out of a  shower stall behind me and wastes no  time yanking the door open and fumbling  my way through the next room in the dark  this leads me back to the original  mirror room the elevator car from the  ride is now there seemingly just waiting  for me the creepy bellhop guy is in the  same seat continuing to stare me down I  don't even bother to stop running across  the mirror room through the door on the  other side now I'm in another hotel  corridor but different from the one  upstairs at the end of the hall I see a  woman and yet another bellhop character  this one wearing a red pair of Mickey  Mouse ears with an Iron Man logo on it  the two were having a dispute she's  screaming and grabbing onto the sides of  the doorframe as he violently tries to  pull her out of the room she's screaming  please don't make me go and he would  just methodically respond by telling her  that her stay is up and she's welcome to  check into one of their other hotels he  then yanked her hard enough for her to  lose grip on the door and she flew  across the hallway crashing her head on  the wall hard enough to draw blood she  collapsed on the floor in front of him  that's when he looked up and noticed me  with the same intense stare that the  bellhops down in the lobby  given us my vision was starting to get  blurry so I decided to go into one of  the rooms to see if I could buy myself  some time I assumed that all the doors  were fakes but was pleasantly surprised  when one of them actually opened leading  to yet another corridor I was too tired  to try to comprehend how this was  possible given the layout of the ride  and given the fact that these secret  rooms have no reason to exist in the  first place just then the room went dark  and the walls floor and ceiling became  projection map with the starry night sky  the same effect used in the second floor  of the actual version of the ride at the  end was a single door I took this is the  metaphorical exit to the twilight zone  so I ran to it as fast as I could as I  was running I heard the narrator's  booming voice one last time next time  you try to mess with history make sure  you know just what kind of things you're  filling or you may find a few nasty  surprises coming your way you may or may  not have made it through tonight but to  close this door is to forever live on in  your head in Twilight Zone and just like  that it was over the sound of the thirty  soundtrack played in my ears and I was  making my way down the stairs trying to  think about 